  v2 seed     apply: {"ok":false,"blocked":true,"error":"[Immer] Patching reserved attributes ...","immer_version":"9.0.6"}   check: {"polluted":null,"immer_version":"9.0.6"}

DIFFERENTIAL MATRIX (polluted = fresh ({}).isAdmin === true over HTTP; flag iff polluted)
  version          seed ["__proto__","isAdmin"]           residual [["__proto__"],"isAdmin"]
  V0 7.0.15        polluted=true   FLAG                    polluted=true   FLAG
  V1 8.0.1         polluted=false  null (die 24)           polluted=true   FLAG   <-- RESIDUAL
  V2 9.0.6         polluted=false  null (die 24)           polluted=false  null (die 24)

ISOLATION
  Prototype pollution persists for the life of the node process, so oracle.run_probe RESTARTS the target
  container (fresh process => clean Object.prototype) BEFORE each POST -- the seed and the residual (and
  all three versions) are each measured against a fresh process. Confirmed genuine external HTTP flow
  (curl POST /apply then curl GET /check across the published container port).

DATA-QUALITY (all distinct, real differential): V1(8.0.1) != V0(7.0.15); original(string) blocked on V1
while residual(nested-array) passes on V1; residual differs from original; residual blocked on V2. No same
fixed_version (8.0.1 vs 9.0.6), no V1==V0, no original==residual, V1 does NOT block the residual. Distinct
advisories/commits (GHSA-33f9-j839-rf8h vs GHSA-c36v-fmgq-m8hx). Legitimate.

TEARDOWN: `docker compose --profile v0 --profile v1 --profile v2 down -v` (run at end of --run-gate), then
`PCB_FLAG=teardown docker compose ... down -v --rmi all` + `docker image prune -f`. node:18-slim base
kept. Case dir is TEXT only (no node_modules; npm install happens inside the image at build time).

